From 9be5b70e1a747c2fe34cddc0d0324f1b0f06ae23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 02:07:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 022/137] Unified: default names of new objects in the user's
 language
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New bodies, sketches and PartDesign features get their default label in
the user's language (部品, スケッチ, 押し出し001, ...), as origins and datums
already do. Only a label that is still the English default is changed;
internal names stay the same, and undoing the creation removes the object
in one step as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
